>>
endobj
724 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 458 0 R
/E (Lord Jesus, I come to You today taking full authority over my thought life. I recognize that the mind is one of the primary battlefields where the enemy wages war, and I refuse to let him have any territory in my thinking. Your Word says in Romans 12:2 that I am to be transformed by the renewing of my mind, and that is exactly what I am asking You to do in me today. Renew my mind, Lord. Strengthen my thoughts. Guard the gate of my imagination and let nothing enter that does not come from You.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
725 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 458 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
726 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 458 0 R
/E (I come against anxiety. I come against racing thoughts that steal my sleep and rob my peace. I come against intrusive thoughts, dark imaginations, and every mental attack the enemy sends my way. I declare that my mind belongs to You, Lord, and that You have not given me a spirit of fear but of power, love, and a sound mind. I receive that sound mind right now. I receive clarity, focus, and the peace of God that surpasses all understanding.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
727 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 458 0 R
/E (Let Your peace guard my heart and my mind through Christ Jesus. Protect my thinking today. Let every thought I have lead me closer to You rather than further away. Saturate my mind with Your Word, Your truth, and Your perspective on every situation I face. I am protected in my mind because I am hidden in You.)
/Pg 18 0 R
