1343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 552 0 R
/E (I declare my testimony today. I declare that I came from a hard place and God brought me through. I declare that I was in situations that should have broken me and they did not. I declare that there were seasons when I had nothing left and God showed up and showed out in ways that I am still processing. I declare that the same God who moved in my past is moving in my present and will move in my future.)
/Pg 112 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 552 0 R
/E (Lord, help me to use my testimony. Revelation 12:11 says that the saints overcame the accuser by the blood of the Lamb and the word of their testimony. My testimony is a weapon. It is a tool for the Kingdom. When I share openly what You have brought me through, I give someone else the courage to believe that You can do the same for them.)
/Pg 112 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 552 0 R
/E (Let me never be too proud to share my story. Let me never be too polished to talk about where I came from. Let me never be too far along to remember how far I have come and the God who carried me every step of the way. My testimony belongs to You, Lord, and I give it back to You to use for Your glory however You see fit.)
/Pg 112 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
